From: "David S. Miller" <davem@davemloft.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Jul 2012 18:35:12 -0700
Subject: ipv4: Deliver ICMP redirects to sockets too.
Patch-mainline: v3.6-rc1
Git-commit: d3351b75a7169337877fe6f6f2c019154b6ec1ea
References: CVE-2026-46266 bsc#1267684

And thus, we can remove the ping_err() hack.

Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
Acked-by: Michal Kubecek <mkubecek@suse.cz>

---
 net/ipv4/icmp.c | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/net/ipv4/icmp.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/icmp.c
@@ -785,13 +785,7 @@ static void icmp_redirect(struct sk_buff *skb)
 		break;
 	}
 
-	/* Ping wants to see redirects.
-         * Let's pretend they are errors of sorts... */
-	if (iph->protocol == IPPROTO_ICMP &&
-	    iph->ihl >= 5 &&
-	    pskb_may_pull(skb, (iph->ihl<<2)+8)) {
-		ping_err(skb, icmp_hdr(skb)->un.gateway);
-	}
+	icmp_socket_deliver(skb, icmp_hdr(skb)->un.gateway);
 
 out:
 	return;
